    "result_text": "The full suite (AcceptanceTest plus its base) is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `capacityWarning` field with minimal structural impact:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `capacityWarning` boolean (readOnly) to the Owner schema, which generates the DTO getter/setter.\n\n2. **`CityCapacity.java`** (new, small cohesive class) \u2014 `approaching(owners, owner)` returns true when the owner's city holds 40\u201349 owners (`>= 40 && < 50`), reusing the existing `CityCodes.count` helper. It has essentially no surrounding complexity (WMC_other \u2248 0).\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.getOwner`** \u2014 one added line, setting `capacityWarning` on the DTO alongside the other collection-derived fields (membershipPoints, possibleDuplicate) that are already computed there from `findAllOwners()`. This is why the warning survives a fresh `GET` (the field is transient/non-persisted, so it's recomputed on read, matching the existing pattern).\n\nThe hard rejection at 50 in `addOwner` (`CityCodes.count(owners, owner) >= 50` \u2192 `409 CONFLICT`) is untouched. I kept every edited method simple and avoided growing the large controller/model \u2014 the only controller change is a single line, and the real logic lives in a new tiny class.",
